backend/alloy_crew/models/training_data/
# ...except the three sets that are actually load-bearing. They were previously
# force-added past this rule, so `git check-ignore` disagreed with the tree and
# a `git add -A` after a retrain would silently skip them. Together ~0.4 MB.
#
# The models in saved_models/ and saved_models_v2/ are tracked binaries; without
# their training rows nobody can reproduce or re-fit them, and
# evaluation/prediction/scripts/verify_training_provenance.py checks the shipped
# models against these exact files.
!backend/alloy_crew/models/training_data/train_77alloys_v2.jsonl
!backend/alloy_crew/models/training_data/train_77alloys.jsonl
!backend/alloy_crew/models/training_data/final_alloy_data_enriched.jsonl

