backend/scrape/*.py
backend/alloy_crew/*.jsonl
backend/alloy_crew/README.md

# Paper source (authoritative copy lives in Overleaf; never commit)
paper_src/

# Local virtualenv (1.6 GB, 53k files)
.new/

# Stale duplicate of the canonical ontology/alloygraph.owl — the two have
# diverged; ontology/ is the tracked source of truth. Root-anchored: git has
# core.ignorecase=true on macOS, so a bare "Data/" also swallows
# evaluation/prediction/data/, which holds the live evaluation sets.
/Data/

# Superseded evaluation data, mirrors the existing backend/_archive rule
evaluation/_archive/

# Staging bundle for the figshare upload. Every file duplicates something
# already tracked under evaluation/ or ontology/, and the published copy
# lives at doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.31860466.
figshare-data/
alloygraph-data.zip

# Stale paper copies — paper_src/ (Overleaf) is authoritative.
docs/paper.tex
docs/paper-acta.tex
docs/cover-letter.tex
docs/paper/*.md

# Rendered figures under docs/paper/figures are ignored by default: most are
# throwaway exports that go stale the moment the .drawio beside them is edited.
# One such export shipped a wrong alloy count ("99 Ni superalloys") for months
# while its source already said 88.
#
# The three the manuscript actually compiles are exceptions and ARE tracked.
# paper_src/ is git-ignored (Overleaf is authoritative), so without these the
# only copy of each lived on one laptop. kg.png matters most: it is a GraphDB
# screenshot with no source file and a non-deterministic view, so the PNG is
# the artefact of record and losing it loses the figure outright.
docs/paper/figures/*.png
# Figure 1's PNG is NOT here: the manuscript compiles the PDF below, and the
# only consumer of the raster is the README, so the single tracked copy lives
# at assets/system_architecture.png. There used to be a byte-identical second
# copy in this directory (2.5 MB each); re-exports had to update both, and the
# manifest's "four files move together" warning existed only because of it.
!docs/paper/figures/system_architecture.pdf
# The vector export of figure 1. KBS asks for vector artwork, so this, not the
# PNG, is what goes to the publisher. Regenerate with the drawio CLI; see the
# asset manifest.
!docs/paper/figures/agent_pipeline.png
!docs/paper/figures/kg.png

# Generated manuscript assets — regenerate with evaluation/paper_assets/*.py.
# Anchored: an unanchored "paper_assets/" also matches evaluation/paper_assets,
# which holds the generators and must stay tracked. Same trap that previously
# hid evaluation/*/scripts/ behind "scripts/" and evaluation/prediction/data
# behind "Data/".
/paper_assets/
